 ## Background
-Gaussian Avatar was introduced as a method to reconstruct full-body avatars using the SMPL model as a prior [S1][S2, unofficial]. It builds on the principles of Gaussian Splatting and parametric human models [S1]. The method uses pose features to predict Gaussian parameters through a feed-forward network [S2, unofficial]. It is part of the broader family of Gaussian Avatar Reconstruction methods [Parent](8385-smpl-based-rigid-non-rigid-deformation.md) [S1].
+Gaussian Avatar was introduced as a method to leverage the SMPL model as a prior to reconstruct full-body avatars [S1][S2, unofficial]. It uses pose features to predict Gaussian parameters through a feed-forward network [S1][S2, unofficial]. It is part of the broader family of learning and training methods for splatting, building on [Splatting](23-splatting.md) by treating volumetric data as parametric primitives transformed and rasterized [S1][S2, unofficial].
 
